{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Therefore you shall not bring.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted לכן as an expression of oath, as it is said (I Samuel 3:14): ״לכן נשבעתי לבית עלי״ — 'therefore I swore to the house of Eli.' The Holy One, blessed be He, swore that they would not enter the land. And even though Moshe knew this, he did not refrain from carrying out his mission regarding the land. This is why Scripture immediately follows with וישלח משה מלאכים מקדש אל מלך אדום — for at Kadesh it was decreed upon him that he would not enter the land, and from Kadesh he sent his emissaries regarding the land."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:34:13.129274305Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}